Subject: [PATCH] D18 item 2: the bench checks an external source's files
 against pinned hashes (streamed SHA-256, sources[].files, refusal of a
 differing file); TEXBAT stays unpinned until its first fetch; D18 RESULTS

bench::sha256_file hashes in 1 MiB blocks (TEXBAT recordings are tens of GB);
bench::is_sha256_hex checks a manifest hash's form. `kshana bench verify-manifest` reads
sources[].files (path, bytes, sha256): a file whose hash or size differs is refused, a
malformed hash or a pinned source with an unhashed file is an error, and an unpinned
source's files are counted as unpinned. tests/bench_external_source_pins.rs checks the
refusal and that the shipped TEXBAT source is well formed (pinned exactly when it lists
files). b-iq.json keeps sha256_pinned false; its note names the files to pin
(cleanStatic.bin, ds1.bin to ds8.bin). The fetch is with the owner: the data host failed
TLS verification here and was not fetched around it.

docs/design/evidence/d18-bench-leftovers/RESULTS.md records item 1 (built, acceptance
passed) and item 2 (code done, hashes pending).
